<p class="where-in">revival-changes.md, &ldquo;Numbers&rdquo;, line 82, its last sentence</p>
<p>Where the tied declarations differ only <span class="cut">where the call passes a numeral,</span> <span class="add">at the positions of the call's numerals,</span> the checker reads the numeral as <code>ZZ32</code>, or <code>ZZ64</code> or <code>ZZ</code> where the value does not fit.</p>
</div></div>
<div class="note"><p><strong>Why.</strong> &ldquo;Differ only where the call passes a numeral&rdquo; could mean that the declarations differ only at the numeral's position, or only when a numeral is passed. The first is meant, and the text now says so.</p></div>
